(Regression test: arguments's all must be iterable WITHOUT any flag
 schema declared. The filtered view is only populated by the flag-parse
 routine, which is skipped entirely when a program declares no flags -
 previously that left _parsed_argc at 0 forever, so every each-from
 loop and For-each over arguments's all silently ran zero times. The
 runtime now falls back to the raw argv[1..] view until flag parsing
 marks the filtered view valid.)

Print "count: {arguments's count}".

(statement form)
For each item in arguments's all,
    Print "for: {item}".

(loop expansion form)
Print each item from arguments's all.

(function call expansion form - the shape of a coreutils rmdir/cat)
To "shout" of a text called "path".
  Print "fn: {path}".

"shout" of each item from arguments's all.
Print "end".
